1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludwig_Schames Ludwig was born in Frankfurt on August 11th, 1852 as the second child of Isaac and Jeanette Schames. At the age of 19 he left his hometown in order to work as a banker i
2 CONC n Paris. He was interested in contemporary French art which he also collected.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1880 he married Fanny Lewisohn from Hamburg in Paris. Their first child Leon was born in Paris in 1882. In 1885/86 the family returned to Frankfurt where their daughter Martha was born in the Ostendstraße 12 on February 3rd 188
2 CONC 6. Ludwig travelled frequently, to Paris and Hamburg amongst various other places. Between 1885 and 1895 he lived in various places in Frankfurt, but always in the east end of town: Ostendstrasse, Rückertstrasse, Uhlandstrasse, Se
2 CONC ilerstrasse, Hanauer Landstrasse, to be near the Orthodox synagogues. Here his wife Fanny died at the age of 35 in 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the same year Ludwig moved to Baumweg with his children , then 13 and 9 years old, and in 1913 to Wittelsbacher Allee 7. There he lived with Leon, with his removed daughter Martha and her husband Lion Marx and their children, A
2 CONC enne, born in 1910, and Gretel Clara, born in 1914. Ludwig died here on July 3rd 1922.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Ludwig Schames had returned to Frankfurt from Paris in 1895, he knew that he wanted to be active as an art dealer. In the same year he had founded the art trading gallery „Posen & Schames“, together with a colleague, at Opern
2 CONC platz 10.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1906 on he ran the gallery on his own which he now called „Art Salon Schames“. In 1913 he moved to Boersenstrasse 2. Ludwig Schames first showed French Impressionists. From early on he supported Picasso and Max Beckmann who w
2 CONC orked in Frankfurt from 1915 onwards.
2 CONT
2 CONT After World War I the Art Salon Schames became an important centre of German expressionism. One of its most important artists, Ernst Ludwig Kirchner, Schames met personally. In 1916 he showed the first single exhibition of the art
2 CONC ist, in 1919 his complete work in his gallery. Further exhibitions followed, even after the death of Ludwig Schames in 1922. On the occasion of the death of his business partner and friend Ludwig Schames, the artist Kirchner publi
2 CONC shed in the art magazine “Querschnitt” the wood engraving portrait of Ludwig Schames which he had made in 1918 and said farewell with the following words: “This was the art dealer Ludwig Schames, the fine and unselfish friend of t
2 CONC he art and the artists. He enabled others creativity and life in the noblest/most noble way/kind“.
