1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Death record: http://www.holocaust.cz/en/database-of-victims/victim/81623-salomon-ehrenfeld/
2 CONT * Born 24. 03. 1878
2 CONT * Last residence before deportation: Prague V
2 CONT * Address/place of registration in the Protectorate: Prague V, Norimberská 21
2 CONT * Transport At, no. 189 (07. 05. 1942, Prague -> Terezín)
2 CONT * Murdered 14. 11. 1943 Terezín
2 CONT
2 CONT Testimony: http://yvng.yadvashem.org/nameDetails.html?language=en&itemId=5642653
2 CONT * Salomon Ehrenfeld was born in Prenzlau, Germany in 1878 to Khaim and Itel. He was a linguist and married. Prior to WWII he lived in Prague, Czechoslovakia. During the war he was in Terezin, Czechoslovakia.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Salomon was murdered in the Shoah.
2 CONT
2 CONT * This information is based on a Page of Testimony (displayed here) submitted by his son, Nakhum Ehrenfeld
2 CONT
2 CONT Cremated in Terezin
