1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Book details found via Google:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hagode zur Vermählungs-Feier des Fräulein Nenle Weinberg mit Herrn Jacob Posen am 11. Siwan 5644 1884 - Epithalamia - 14 pages
2 CONT
2 CONT A parody of the Haggadah written in honor of the marriage celebration of Jacob Posen (1857-1924) and Nenle (Nelli) Weinberg (born 1863) on June 4, 1884. Jacob Posen was a "Kursmakler" ("exchange broker") in Frankfurt am Main. Nenl
2 CONC e was born in Nottingham, England, and married Jacob on May 25, 1884. Jacob was the honorary dayan of the "Grosse Gemeinde" and mohel. He was active for the Börneplatz Synagogue and the Hermesweg Synagogue. (Source: Arnsberg, Paul
2 CONC . Die Geschichte der Frankfurter Juden seit der französischen Revolution, 1983. Volume 3)
2 CONT
2 CONT Nenle and Jacob Posen had a son referred to in Harry Judah Weinberg's will:
2 CONT 5 October 1923 - Nottingham Evening Post:
2 CONT "Mr Harry Judah Weinberg of 4 North-road, The Park, Nottingham, a member of the firm of Simon, May ........ who died on July1st, aged 48 .......
2 CONT The testator gives ........£2000 upon trust for his nephew Sali Posen, ....."
