1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eintrag im »Gedenkbuch« des Bundesarchivs:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Felsenthal, Friedrich Fritz
2 CONT
2 CONT * geboren am 04. August 1869 
2 CONT * in Aachen/Rheinprovinz
2 CONT
2 CONT * wohnhaft in Aachen 
2 CONT
2 CONT * INTERNIERUNG/INHAFTIERUNG
2 CONT * 00.00.1942 - 28. Mai 1942, 
2 CONT * Buchenwald, Konzentrationslager
2 CONT * TODESDATUM
2 CONT * 28. Mai 1942
2 CONT * TODESORT
2 CONT * Buchenwald, Konzentrationslager
2 CONT
2 CONT cf.: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liste_der_Stolpersteine_in_Aachen
2 CONT
2 CONT Fritz Felsenthal was a brother of Erich Felsenthal. He was born in Aachen on the 4 August 1869. He was very assimilated and could speak Öcher Platt, the Aachen dialect. He felt very German, and liked to go to the pub with his Aach
2 CONC en friends. He felt safe, and didnt try to emigrate. In 1941 he was taken to Buchenwald, and on 29 May 1942 he died there. His ashes were returned to Aachen, and one of his friends buried the ashes on the jewish Aachen cemetery. T
2 CONC hey also put a plaque over the grave. Fritz has a Stolperstein in the street in front of the house where the Felsenthal's lived before the war. 
