1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanns_Alexander
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Hanns Alexander (1917–2006) was a German Jewish refugee who tracked down and arrested the Kommandant of Auschwitz Rudolf Höss.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Berlin to father Alfred Alexander and mother Henny Alexander, he grew up in Nazi Germany. In 1936 the family fled to England.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1940, he joined the Royal Pioneer Corps and in 1945 he became an interpreter for the No. 1 War Crimes Investigation Team at Belsen.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Later that year he became a full-time Nazi hunter who tracked down and arrested Gustav Simon and Rudolf Höss.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT After the War he had a long professional career as a merchant banker at S.G. Warburg. Hanns Alexander died in London at age 89.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT His story is featured in the book Hanns and Rudolf by Thomas Harding.
