2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/articles/A48727-2005Feb23.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Physicist, Metrologist H. Steffen Peiser Dies
2 CONT
2 CONT By Yvonne Shinhoster Lamb
2 CONT
2 CONT Washington Post Staff Writer
2 CONT
2 CONT Thursday, February 24, 2005; Page B05 
2 CONT
2 CONT H. Steffen Peiser, 87, a chemist and a physicist who was the international liaison with what is now the National Institute of Standards and Technology, died Feb. 10 at his home in Asbury Methodist Village in Gaithersburg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Peiser joined the former National Bureau of Standards in 1957, working first as a bench scientist in the field of crystallography. He directed the mass and scale section beginning in 1959, and in 1962 he was appointed chief of
2 CONC  the crystal chemistry section. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Search Paid Death Notices 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Call (202) 334-4122 to place a paid death notice. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Search Death Notices:  
2 CONT
2 CONT Death notices are searchable for 30 days. Leave field blank and click "Go" to see full list. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Share memories about friends and loved ones in the Guest books. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The help page has more information.   
2 CONT
2 CONT _____Obituary Submissions_____ 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Visit the obituary information page to learn about news obituary and death notice submissions. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Free E-mail Newsletters
2 CONT
2 CONT Today's Headlines & Columnists
2 CONT
2 CONT See a Sample  |  Sign Up Now 
