1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Heinrich Eisner
2 CONT Worldwide Jewish Burial Registry from JewishGen
2 CONT Birth:	Sep 30 1850
2 CONT Death:	Aug 12 1918
2 CONT Burial:	Aug 15 1918 - Jüdischer Friedhof Weiáensee, Berlin, Germany
2 CONT Wife:	Olga Tarlau
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich Eisner
2 CONT Famous People Throughout History
2 CONT Birth:	1850
2 CONT Death:	1918
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c33pvlez6yjo
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich Eisner helped build the Hahn'sche Werke steel business into one of the most high-tech and sprawling companies in central Europe.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the turn of the 20th Century, Heinrich was one of the wealthiest businessmen in Germany - the equivalent of a modern multi-billionaire.
2 CONT
2 CONT His company manufactured tubular steel, with factories spread across Germany, Poland and Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich, and his wife, Olga, owned several properties in and around Berlin, including an impressive six-storey property in the city centre with marble floors and a cream-white façade.
2 CONT
2 CONT When he died in 1918, Heinrich left shares in his company - and his personal fortune - to his son Rudolf, recently returned from fighting in World War One.
