1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marianne's Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT Bedminster
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marianne Goldsmith 90, was born in Saalfeld, East Prussia, Germany on December 5, 1923, the only child of Gertrude and Ludwig Michaelis. Marianne emigrated to the United States in 1935 on Columbus Day, 1935 and lived in Queens wi
2 CONC th her parents. Marianne was a 1946 graduate of Cornell University, School of Home Economics (now Human Ecology). She worked as a case worker after graduation and in 1949 married her long time sweetheart, Karl. They lived in New J
2 CONC ersey for their entire married life – briefly in New Brunswick and then in Middlesex until moving to Plainfield in 1966. Marianne and Karl moved to their current home in Bedminster in 1986. Marianne worked as a substitute teacher,
2 CONC  studied library science and became a school librarian at Washington School in Plainfield and also taught psychology at North Plainfield High School Throughout her adult life, Marianne volunteered at her children's schools, her sy
2 CONC nagogue, was a hospice volunteer and a lifetime member of Hadassah. She was a lover of the arts, particularly classical music and opera as well as non-fiction, especially biographies. Marianne had a tremendous love of learning and
2 CONC  love of people. Marianne's husband, Karl, predeceased her in 2002 as well as her eldest son, Michael in 2008. She is survived by her three children Laurie, Jody and Melanie, spouses of her children Linda, Saul, Amira and Joel and
2 CONC  her 11 grandchildren Jacob, Marla, Sarah, Adam, Gary, Max, Wendy, Sam, Trudianne, Henry and Rebecca. Funeral services will be 11am Tuesday at Congregation B'nai, 40 Whitenack Road Basking Ridge. Interment will follow at Cedar Par
2 CONC k Cemetery, Paramus. Arrangements by Bruce C VanArsdale Funeral Home, Somerville Donations to: Bridgewater YMCA, 601 Garretson Road, Bridgewater, NJ 08807, Clarence Dillon Library, Bedminster, NJ 07921, Cornell University Plantati
2 CONC ons, 1 Plantation Road, Ithaca, NY 14850, Congregation B'nai Israel, 40 Whitenack Road, Basking Ridge, NJ 07920
