2 DATE 2 JAN 1967
2 PLAC New York, NY, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Schames, Samson, (1898-1967), The Gate Internment Camp at Huyton near Liverpool (1940)
2 CONT
2 CONT Samson Schames came from an old Frankfurt family. Trained in the Staedelschule, he stood at the beginning of his career when National Socialism began. After emigrating to London he created collages and mosaics from found materials
2 CONC  and debris, which urgently convey the greyness and destruction under bombardment and during his internment in the Huyton Alien Internment Camp. The works created a breakthrough at that time in their bold forms for abstraction.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WQLZ9LeQcHE
