1 NOTE 5/9/2004:
2 CONT The son, Fritz Siegfried, left Germany after Kristallnact in 1938 and went to Holland then England, where he and his wife Edith stayed until coming to New York in 1949. He was an artist and mosaic maker. In England he started usin
2 CONC g the name Samson instead of Fritz.  He died in 1967.(His wife is still alive and living in NYC. In 1989, the Jewish Museum in Frankfurt
2 CONT had a major exhibition of his work.   I have the
2 CONT catalog from that show and that is where my other information comes from.  It says, on a page printed from some of his writings that his mother was deported to Theresienstadt in September 1942, and died there in February, 1943. It
2 CONC  also says that his sister "vanished and was never heard of" during this time. Since I only recently looked at this catalog after many years, I will take the opportunity next time I am in Frankfurt (where I travel occasionally wit
2 CONC h my husband who does some business there)to see whether they are listed on the Memorial at the old Jewish cemetery. I have also been at the (newer) Frankfurt cemetery where they have a listing for a Paul Isaak Schames, buried Sep
2 CONC t.7,
2 CONT 1936 and I assume this is the other brother.
2 CONT My husband's great-grandfather Ludwig Schames was a brother of Albert Schames. Ludwig was a prominent Frankfurt art dealer who was a patron of German Expressionists, particularly Ernst Ludwig Kirschner.
2 CONT I hope this information is of use to you. I only recently got started in doing family history....your family listing on JewishGen is certainly an
2 CONT inspiration!   Harriet Mayer
