2 CONT Mozes Hartog Hirsch Lehren‏‎
2 CONT
2 CONT Born ‎1747 Meissenheim, died ‎3 Jan 1815 The Hague, Abraham-Moshe Lehren died on 21 Teveth 5575 and was buried on 22 Teveth in The Hague.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was dayan & pu"m in The Hague - see: S. Seeligman in 'Catalog der reichhaltigen Sammlung hebraischer u. judischer Bucher, Handschriften etc, nachgelassen von N.H. van Biema in Amsterdam, 1904.‎, 67 or 68 years. Son of Hirsch Ak
2 CONC iba Lehren and Gelle Uri-Peis Kanstat‏
2 CONT
2 CONT Married ‎1782 Amsterdam, dtb 753/173; witn.groom: David Salomon; witn.bride: f.Benedictus Dushness. Engaged ‎Feb 1782 Amsterdam On 3 Shevat 5542 an act is made up before the trustees of the jewish community in The Hague, wherein t
2 CONC he wonderful bachelor, faultless and elevated in the tora requirements and well versed therein as well, khr"r Moshe b"h Zwi Hirsch, names and authorises the rabbi, the great and reknown genius mohr"r Sha'ul, chief rabbi of kille k
2 CONC odesh Amsterdam to connect him [in engagement] with the well versed maiden Jettel, daughter of the wonderful rabbani mho' Baruch Bendit Dushnith-Segal, who lives in Amsterdam, and intends to engage his daughter Jettel in marriage 
2 CONC according to the law of Mozes & Israel; signed by hak' Moshe Lehren from Mannheim. Tnaim rishonim in act 5542/13 on 6 Shevat 5542; the great and reknown genius, his generation's example mohr"r Sha'ul m.h.l, chiefrabbi of our commu
2 CONC nity, who comes on behalf of and amply authorised by the faultless bachelor, the wonderful torani k"h Moshe ben k"h Hirsch z.l, as authorised on last 3 Cheshvan before the trustees of the jewish community of The Hague; the wonderf
2 CONC ul torani rabbani mohr"r Bendit ben hr"r Shlomo Dushnit-Segal z.l, who comes on behalf of his daughter the dear and well versed maiden Jettele; the bride's father will donate fl. 700,- to the dowry; intended chuppa in Amsterdam in
2 CONC  the month Adar of 5543; committed for groom: aluf katsin mefursam k"h Ephraim Tiel m.h.l. from The Hague, as specified in the authorisation act; committed for bride: katsin torani mefursam pu hr"r Leib Norden m.h.l. to:
2 CONT
2 CONT  reports
2 CONT  ‎womanJudith Jettele Benedictus Bendit Dushness‏‎ Born ‎± 1755 Prague, died ‎MRT 1821 The Hague, Lea-Jettele bat mho' Bendit Dushnith, died on 20 Adar 5581 in The Hague and was buried there. Died on 13 Mar 1822 and was buried on 
2 CONC 21 Adar 5582 (14 Mar 1822) - according to mr. Jan Vegers‎, approximately 66 years. Occupation: The Hague, kept shop in cottonware in The Hague, St. Jacobstr... Daughter of Benedictus Baruch-Bendit Salomon Shlomo Dushness and Ester
2 CONC  Meyer Margalioth‏
