2 DATE 13 JUL 1989
2 ADDR
3 CITY Huddersfield
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 OCCU Electronic engineer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hans Alfred Mathias - nicknamed Mat'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://www.matamp.com/mat-mathias.html Biography of Mat Mathias from Mat Amps Company Page]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mat Mathias was born in 1923. In 1939 Mat was evacuated to England with the entire school
2 CONT he was attending in Berlin. He was first settled in a camp at Sandwich on the south coast of
2 CONT England and then later moved to Leeds. While in Leeds Mat was in Digs at a private house with some
2 CONT other boys also from the same school. Later on Mat found work in a comb factory, then interned
2 CONT at York Race Course on the Isle of Man.  Mat had a friend in Bradford who found him
2 CONT work in a cinema projection box as a trainee. From there he moved to Huddersfield to work at
2 CONT the Ritz Cinema as the projectionist under a chief.
2 CONT
2 CONT Next Mat bought a share of a business doing Radio Repairs in Albion Street. The original owner
2 CONT wanted to leave so Mat was obliged to take on the whole business and pay for it with what he
2 CONT made each week. Mat did not have any wage left for himself for a long time but eventually the
2 CONT debt was paid off. When television became available Mat went into TV and gradually built up a
2 CONT small business. He did some television repairs for a firm on King Street, in Huddersfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1956 Mat was married and the following year in 1957 he bought the King Street shop and his
2 CONT wife Ruth, worked at King Street whilst he kept doing repairs at the shop on Albion Street.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mat had an apprentice at this time who played guitar and used a Tandberg tape recorder which
2 CONT was part of his Hi-Fi stock. Mat made a recording of his playing. Mat then built up his recording
2 CONT equipment and spent many hours recording the local pop groups. The groups would discuss with
2 CONT Mat what they wanted from an amplifier and Mat would make modifications to their equipment.
2 CONT The King Street Shop became known as MATAMP in 1958, and eventually in 1962 Mat designed
2 CONT a "new" amplifier for the guitar which he called MATAMP.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Dates verified 2006 with Mrs. Mathias."Matamp was not even thought of in 1946, ignore Jeff Lewis."]
2 CONT
