2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Bromberg, Germany (now Bydgoszcz, Poland) on September 17, 1888, Kurt Friedlaender studied law and was a senior official in the provincial government of Pomerania. He emigrated to Great Britain in 1939 and died in London i
2 CONC n 1968. His parents were Martin Friedlaender (1856-1932) and Clara née Friedlaender (1864-circa 1942). He had two brothers, Paul (1885-1886) and Erich (1891-1942). His grandfather, Dagobert Friedlaender (1826-1904) was a member of
2 CONC  the Preussisches Herrenhaus (upper chamber of Prussian parliament).
